{
  "benchmark_id": 224,
  "prompt": "Write a function that takes three parameters, currentIndex, defaultList, and customList. The currentIndex value is a string like \"default-0\" or \"custom-1\" where the part before the hyphen is the list type and the part after the hyphen is the index. Split currentIndex on \"-\" to get the type and index, choose defaultList when the type is \"default\" and customList when the type is \"custom\", and then select the item at that index from the chosen list. Return an object with list (the selected list array), current (the item at that index), and dispatch set to null. \n\n  Only return the code, don't include any other information,\n    such as a preamble or suffix.\n",
  "implementation_details": "Language: JavaScript. Use string selection to choose a list, initialize defaults, and return a dispatch function to update it.",
  "fc_tests": [
    {
      "test_id": 0,
      "input": {
        "currentIndex": "default-0",
        "defaultList": [
          "a",
          "b"
        ],
        "customList": [
          "x"
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": {
        "list": [
          "a",
          "b"
        ],
        "current": "a",
        "dispatch": null
      }
    },
    {
      "test_id": 1,
      "input": {
        "currentIndex": "custom-1",
        "defaultList": [
          "a"
        ],
        "customList": [
          "x",
          "y"
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": {
        "list": [
          "x",
          "y"
        ],
        "current": "y",
        "dispatch": null
      }
    },
    {
      "test_id": 2,
      "input": {
        "currentIndex": "default-1",
        "defaultList": [
          "item1",
          "item2",
          "item3"
        ],
        "customList": [
          "custom1"
        ]
      },
      "expected_output": {
        "list": [
          "item1",
          "item2",
          "item3"
        ],
        "current": "item2",
        "dispatch": null
      }
    },
    {
